   Monitor / Views / Daily / COT tab strip + the CSV action -- the page's primary navigation, measured 52-76x24 at 820px.
   `--tap-min` is 44px and breakpoints.css calls EVERYTHING at or below 1024px
   TOUCH -- phone AND tablet. These are chrome a finger aims at, so they take
   the floor on the whole touch tier.

   ⛔ NOT APPLIED to dense in-table affordances or chart-overlay micro-toggles
   elsewhere on this app: a 44px floor on a data grid's inline controls
   destroys the density the grid exists to provide. That is a per-surface
   design call, not something to sweep. Rail: app/src/styles/tapFloor.test.js. */
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  ._tab_1ckcz_41,
